<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs weaken in U.S. trade, Dow climbs 58 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs weaken in U.S. trade, Dow climbs 58 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were mostly weaker in late U.S. trade, while by 7.35 a.m. NZ time the Dow Jones Industrial Index had climbed 58.53 points to 7,981.51.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S. and</p>
<p>Australia.</p>
<p>Company	  Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg	 N.Y.    US$28/09	  -0/12  *</p>
<p>FCL Engy	 N.Y.    US$31 1/2	 -0 1/2 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper	N.Y.    US$22/05	  -0/05  *</p>
<p>FCL Forest     N.Y.    US$13 1/2	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>MAS Tech	 NASDAQ   US17		 -1</p>
<p>Telecom	  N.Y.    US$40 1/2	 -0 5/8 *</p>
<p>Tranz Rail     N.Y.    US$16 1/8	 +0 1/8 *</p>
<p>Lion	    Sydney  A$3.42		-7</p>
<p>Goodman	 Sydney  A$1.80		nil</p>
<p>Macraes	 Sydney  A$1.45		-5</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of eight shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
